INT. NIGHT BUS - MOVING - NIGHT

Route 9, last run. Sodium light strobes through rain-streaked windows. Three passengers and a driver nobody can see.

CLOSE ON a gym bag on the back seat. Zipper half open. Cash.

JUNO MARCHETTI, 30s, rumpled blazer, sits clutching that bag like a toddler. Beside the aisle, SAM OKONKWO-REID, late 20s, they/them, buzzcut and a vintage bomber jacket, eats cold fries and watches Juno with a grin. Across from them, BERNIE KOWALCZYK, 60s, big coat, bigger moustache, sleeps.

SAM
You've been gripping that bag since Harlow Street. Are you carrying a baby or a bomb?

JUNO
It's a gym bag.

SAM
Sweetheart, nobody sweats that much.

Juno laughs too loud. Bernie stirs. Both of them freeze, then relax when he snores again.

JUNO
(whispering)
Look I need you to stop being charming at me. It's not helping

SAM
Charming is my only setting. They gave me one setting at the factory.

ANGLE ON the bus mirror. The driver's eyes, flat, watching.

The bus LURCHES over a pothole. The bag tips. A brick of cash slides into the aisle. Juno dives, Sam dives, they crack heads, the bag goes sideways, fries everywhere.

JUNO
Ow! Ow, ow

SAM
That was my face!

BERNIE
(eyes closed)
Kids. Keep it down. Some of us have been robbed before and we're trying to rest.

Silence. Juno and Sam stare at him.

BERNIE (CONT'D)
(opening one eye)
Relax. I'm retired. I don't care whose money it is.

INSERT - Sam's phone screen: a news alert. BANK ON FERRIS AVE ROBBED, TWO SUSPECTS AT LARGE.

Sam turns the screen to Juno slowly. Juno exhales, sinks into the seat.

JUNO
Okay. Okay. Plan B.

SAM
We had a plan A?

JUNO
Barely.

BACK TO SCENE. The bus slows. Blue light flickers ahead on the wet road. This is the last time the three of them will be calm.

SAM
(grinning anyway)
Well. It's been a pleasure being your accomplice.

Bernie pats the bag, closes his eye again.

BERNIE
Wake me at the courthouse.
